# Response headers for the static asset tree.
#
# The adapter puts its own immutable Cache-Control rule for /_astro/* at the
# top of this file at build time, so what ships is that plus this — read
# dist/client/_headers rather than this file when debugging what was served.

# Discovery, per RFC 8288.
#
# The same two pointers the markup already carries, in the response head, so
# an agent that issues a HEAD request — or reads only the headers of a GET —
# finds the sitemap and the context file without parsing any HTML.
#
# `describedby` is the registered relation for "a resource describing this
# one", which is what llms.txt is. `sitemap` is not in the IANA registry but
# is the long-standing convention, and is the relation the `<link>` in
# BaseLayout already uses; a mismatch between the two would be worse than
# using the conventional token.
#
# One header field with two link-values rather than two fields: both are
# legal, and a single field is the form least likely to be mangled in transit.
#
# This covers the asset tree, which is every route but the four blog ones —
# those are rendered by the Worker, which builds its own response and never
# consults this file.
/*
  Link: </sitemap-index.xml>; rel="sitemap", </llms.txt>; rel="describedby"; type="text/plain"
